{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:53.583205+00:00","comments":[],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary\n\nWhen a `dynamic-update-slice` is partitioned along the updated dimension and its start index is out of range (so HLO semantics clamp it), the SPMD partitioner computes shard ownership from the **raw** start. No shard satisfies the ownership predicate, so the update is silently dropped. The same program compiled on one device (and NumPy) applies the clamped update.  \n\n## Reproducer (CPU and 2 host devices)\n\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ[\"XLA_FLAGS\"] = \"--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=2\"\nos.environ[\"JAX_PLATFORMS\"] = \"cpu\"\nimport numpy as np, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\nfrom jax.sharding import NamedSharding, PartitionSpec as P\n\nmesh = jax.make_mesh((2,), (\"x\",), devices=jax.devices(\"cpu\")[:2])\ncols = NamedSharding(mesh, P(None, \"x\"))   # shard the updated (column) axis\nrep  = NamedSharding(mesh, P())\n\ndef f(x, upd, start):\n    return lax.dynamic_update_slice(x, upd, [jnp.int32(0), start])\n\nx   = jnp.arange(4, dtype=jnp.int32).reshape(2, 2)\nupd = jnp.full((2, 1), 99, jnp.int32)\nstart = jnp.int32(2)          # out of range: HLO clamps it to dim - size = 1\n\nprint(\"unsharded:\", jax.jit(f)(x, upd, start).tolist())\nprint(\"sharded:  \", jax.jit(f, in_shardings=(cols, rep, rep), out_shardings=cols)(x, upd, start).tolist())\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nunsharded: [[0, 99], [2, 99]]\nsharded:   [[0, 1], [2, 3]]      <- update gets silently dropped\n```\nExpected: both `[[0, 99], [2, 99]]` (`DynamicUpdateSlice` clamps `start` into `[0, 2 - 1] = [0, 1]`, so column 1 must be replaced).\n\n","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/comments","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:27:14Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49118","id":5513688169,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Related to XLA on CPU","id":4432378339,"name":"CPU","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABCDC54w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/CPU"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"B04E1E","default":false,"description":"Related to sharding","id":8390615212,"name":"sharding","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAAB9B6grA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/sharding"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABSKQ0aQ","number":49118,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/timeline","title":"[XLA] SPMD partitioner drops a dynamic-update-slice whose start index needs clamping","type":null,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T04:31:48Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70980689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snarang181","id":70980689,"login":"snarang181","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTgwNjg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181","user_view_type":"public"}},"pages":{"comments":[{"page":1,"records":0,"sha256":"37517e5f3dc66819f61f5a7bb8ace1921282415f10551d2defa5c3eb0985b570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/comments?per_page=100&page=1"}],"issue":[{"etag":"\"8c69a907d4dd0005e298d64abd8a0b249a1ffaa7c53cad8a7dd3936f5ff9ee8e\"","last_modified":"Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:31:48 GMT","records":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118"}],"timeline":[{"page":1,"records":8,"sha256":"343060d9873c9110f6ce872f44bc9335875135457a449098c6be5efd21d22859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49118/timeline?per_page=100&page=1"}]},"record_id":"github-openxla-xla-49118","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49118","timeline":[{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70980689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snarang181","id":70980689,"login":"snarang181","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTgwNjg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-19T21:34:23Z","event":"renamed","id":31460666824,"node_id":"RTE_lADOHyx1PM8AAAABSKQ0ac8AAAAHUzOtyA","performed_via_github_app":null,"rename":{"from":"SPMD partitioner drops a dynamic-update-slice whose start index needs clamping","to":"[XLA] SPMD partitioner drops a dynamic-update-slice whose start index needs clamping"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/events/31460666824"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70980689?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snarang181","id":70980689,"login":"snarang181","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTgwNjg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snarang181","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-09-19T21:47:59Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary\n\nFor a `dynamic-slice` whose result is partitioned along the sliced dimension and whose start index is out of range, the SPMD partitioner emits `partition_id * shard_size + clamp(raw_start, 0, dim − slice_size)`, i.e. it clamps the raw start against the whole operand and then adds the shard offset. `DynamicSlice` semantics clamp the *global* start first (here 7 → 2) and each result shard then reads its own piece of that window (starts 2 and 5). The emitted starts are 5 and 5, so both shards return the same last columns. Unsharded compilation and NumPy are correct. Similar to #49118 (dynamic-update-slice). \n\n## Reproducer (CPU only, 2 host devices)\n\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ[\"XLA_FLAGS\"] = \"--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=2\"\nos.environ[\"JAX_PLATFORMS\"] = \"cpu\"\nimport numpy as np, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\nfrom jax.sharding import NamedSharding, PartitionSpec as P\n\nmesh = jax.make_mesh((2,), (\"x\",), devices=jax.devices(\"cpu\")[:2])\ncols = NamedSharding(mesh, P(None, \"x\"))   # shard the sliced (column) axis\nrep  = NamedSharding(mesh, P())\n\ndef f(x, start):\n    return lax.dynamic_slice(x, [jnp.int32(0), start], (2, 6))\n\nx = jnp.arange(16, dtype=jnp.int32).reshape(2, 8)\nstart = jnp.int32(7)                        # out of range: clamps to 8 - 6 = 2 -> columns 2..7\nexpected = np.asarray(x)[:, 2:8]\n\nuns = np.asarray(jax.jit(f)(x, start))\nsh  = np.asarray(jax.jit(f, in_shardings=(cols, rep), out_shardings=cols)(x, start))\nprint(\"unsharded:\", uns[0].tolist(), \"ok\" if np.array_equal(uns, expected) else \"WRONG\")\nprint(\"sharded:  \", sh[0].tolist(),  \"ok\" if np.array_equal(sh, expected) else \"WRONG\")\n```\n\n```\nunsharded: [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] ok\nsharded:   [5, 6, 7, 5, 6, 7] WRONG\n```\n## Agent Analysis\n\nPost-partitioner HLO for the result-shard slice:\n\n```\n%multiply = %partition-id * 3\n%clamp    = clamp(0, %raw_start, 5)        ; clamps against the 8-wide operand (8 - 3)\n%start    = %multiply + %clamp\nROOT dynamic-slice(%global_value, 0, %start), dynamic_slice_sizes={2,3}\n```\n\nFor raw start 7 the clamp gives 5 on both partitions, and the surviving dynamic-slice's own clamp into `[0, 8 − 3]` keeps 5 for both. The correct order is `clamp(raw_start, 0, 8 − 6) = 2`, then `2 + partition_id * 3` → `[2, 5]`. Code: the partitioned-dimension dynamic-slice path in `SpmdPartitioningVisitor::HandleDynamicSlice`, `xla/service/spmd/spmd_partitioner.cc`.\n\n","closed_at":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122/comments","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:47:58Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49122","id":5513823228,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Awaiting response from openxla-eng","id":4409976552,"name":"stat:awaiting openxla-eng","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/stat:awaiting%20openxla-eng"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Related to XLA on CPU","id":4432378339,"name":"CPU","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABCDC54w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/CPU"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"B04E1E","default":false,"description":"Related to sharding","id":8390615212,"name":"sharding","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAAB9B6grA","url":"https://api.githu